  cutscene_lines:
  - There's a saying that the strong are meant to defend the weak and with that comes
    harmony & peace.
  - A world where each one's necessity is fulfilled with freedom aside from perturbation
    and fear.
  - Yet there's not a single day without crime around every corner, families weeping
    out of hardship and suffering.
  - 'What seemed to be the strong to defend the weak, only to

    exploit them for
    triumph and the wealth they seek..'
  - 'Eventually, it comes into question, where does "happiness" truly

    come from..'
  - 'Bags of wealth? The sense of power over something else? Or

    maybe.. just
    maybe..'
  - The will to bring torn pieces back together..
  - ...
  - ( grunt )
  - Another day, another stinkin terrible day..
  - This city just reeks of crime and penury. Even the news agrees with me..
  - How many days has it been since I worked on that minor missing item case? Fifteen?
    Twenty five? Apparently I lost count..
  - Maybe mom was right. This gig prolly ain't for me.
  - I admired dad's work and his principles.. but I never knew him nor can I possibly
    reach his level of intelligence and wisdom..
  - ...
  - As interesting as the world of detectives and crime solving may be, you are just
    at level one. Heh, maybe even a zero.
  - Not to mention the rampant acts of violence lurking in every corner..
  - Rather than out of malevolence, it has turned into a necessity simply to bring
    food to their plate.
  - Lack of job opportunities, terrible state of the economy. Who would even commission
    a detective at this point..
  - (sigh) .. even my mom's working overtime. I'm starting to feel bad for her ..
  - I'm letting go of this mantle tomorrow. There's no use in hoping for a lost cause..
  - Several hours later, you've decided to hit the hay. It was rather a quiet evening..
  - except..
  - ( You received 1 email )
  - 'Did I hear something? (grunts) '
  - An email? From who?
  - '"For Detective Paul Payton"'
  - '"Evening, sire. I got an urgent case that requires your expertise. I''ve witnessed
    your skills before and I know you''''ll be fit for the job."'
  - '"However, I''m yet to tell you my name and there''s much more to discuss. I
    can''t say anything further. They''re all watching.."'
  - '"Meet me at the house near the countryside under these coordinates"'
  - A set of coordinates was written under the previous passage, supposedly pointing
    towards a vacant house in the countryside, distant from the rest of its residents.
  - ...
  - This has to be a joke..
  - ( scrolls down )
  - '"and no, this is not a joke.. ( this message will now delete itself in 5 minutes..
    )"'
  - ... who sent this ?
  - As fishy as it may seem, it's been months since the last commission.. and I do
    need another one. Man.. talk about desperation..
  - I can even pay off several of mom's bills afterwards. Better off than sagging
    away on this old bed.
  - (sigh) I can't believe I'm lying to mom again about this but..
  - It's for the better..
  - ...
  - ( minutes of driving later... )
  - ...
  - ( car door closes )
  - ...
  - This must be the place the stranger was talking about..
  - ( knock )
  - Hello? Anyone home?
  - ...
  - ( knock )
  - Hello?
  - Wait a minute. The door's unlocked..
  - But noone else is aware of this address other than me. It's literally in the
    middle of nowhere..
  - ( puts ear against door )
  - It's too quiet. Something's off..
  - ( I should try to investigate.. )
